("What are the major rivers of India?","Major rivers: Ganga, Yamuna, Brahmaputra, Indus, Godavari (the longest in South India, the 'Dakshin Ganga'), Krishna, Kaveri, Narmada and Tapi (these two flow west into the Arabian Sea), and Mahanadi.",["rivers of india","major rivers in india","longest river in south india","dakshin ganga","west flowing rivers"]),
("Where does the Ganga start?","The Ganga starts at the Gangotri Glacier (Gaumukh) in Uttarakhand as the Bhagirathi. It joins the Alaknanda at Devprayag to become the Ganga, and flows into the Bay of Bengal, forming the Sundarbans delta with the Brahmaputra.",["origin of ganga","source of ganges","gangotri"]),
("What are the mountain ranges of India?","Mountain ranges: the Himalayas (north), Karakoram, Aravalli (among the oldest in the world), Vindhya and Satpura (central), Western Ghats (Sahyadri) and Eastern Ghats. The Nilgiris are where the Western and Eastern Ghats meet.",["mountain ranges of india","oldest mountain range in india","aravalli","western ghats","eastern ghats"]),
("What are the famous national parks in India?","Famous national parks: Jim Corbett (Uttarakhand, India's first, 1936), Kaziranga (Assam, one-horned rhinos), Gir (Gujarat, the only home of Asiatic lions), Sundarbans (West Bengal, tigers in mangroves), Ranthambore (Rajasthan), Bandipur (Karnataka) and Mudumalai (Tamil Nadu).",["national parks in india","first national park in india","gir national park","kaziranga","asiatic lion"]),
("What is the Tropic of Cancer?","The Tropic of Cancer (23.5° N) passes through 8 Indian states: Gujarat, Rajasthan, Madhya Pradesh, Chhattisgarh, Jharkhand, West Bengal, Tripura and Mizoram.",["tropic of cancer","tropic of cancer india"]),
("What are the types of soil in India?","Main soils in India: alluvial (river plains, most fertile, most widespread), black or regur (Deccan, good for cotton), red (Tamil Nadu, Karnataka), laterite (hilly, rainy areas), desert and mountain soils.",["soils of india","black soil","alluvial soil","red soil","types of soil"]),
("What is the monsoon?","The monsoon is a seasonal wind that brings most of India's rain. The south-west monsoon (June–September) reaches Kerala around 1 June. Tamil Nadu gets most of its rain from the north-east monsoon (October–December).",["monsoon","southwest monsoon","northeast monsoon","rainy season india"]),
("Which is the wettest place in India?","Mawsynram in Meghalaya is one of the wettest places on Earth, with nearby Cherrapunji (Sohra) close behind.",["wettest place in india","mawsynram","cherrapunji","highest rainfall in india"]),
("Which is the coldest place in India?","Dras in Ladakh is one of the coldest inhabited places in India, where winter temperatures can drop below −40 °C.",["coldest place in india","dras"]),
("What are the neighbouring countries of India?","India's neighbours by land: Pakistan, China, Nepal, Bhutan, Bangladesh, Myanmar and Afghanistan (through the Pakistan-occupied area). By sea: Sri Lanka and the Maldives. India shares its longest border with Bangladesh.",["neighbouring countries of india","india neighbours","countries bordering india"]),
("What are the famous lakes of India?","Famous lakes: Chilika (Odisha, the largest coastal lagoon), Wular (J&K, the largest freshwater lake), Dal (Srinagar), Loktak (Manipur, with floating islands), Sambhar (Rajasthan, the largest salt lake), and Vembanad (Kerala, the longest lake).",["lakes of india","largest lake in india","chilika lake","largest freshwater lake in india","dal lake"]),
("What is the Palk Strait?","The Palk Strait separates Tamil Nadu from Sri Lanka. Ram Setu (Adam's Bridge), a chain of limestone shoals, lies between Rameswaram's Pamban Island and Mannar Island.",["palk strait","ram setu","adams bridge"]),
("What are the major ports of India?","Major ports: Mumbai, Jawaharlal Nehru Port (Navi Mumbai, the busiest container port), Kandla/Deendayal (Gujarat), Chennai, V.O. Chidambaranar (Thoothukudi), Kochi, Visakhapatnam, Paradip and Kolkata. Mundra is the largest private port.",["ports of india","major ports in india","largest port in india"]),
("What are the famous waterfalls in India?","Famous waterfalls: Jog Falls (Karnataka), Dudhsagar (Goa), Athirappilly (Kerala, 'Niagara of India'), Hogenakkal (Tamil Nadu), Courtallam (Tamil Nadu, 'Spa of South India'), Nohkalikai (Meghalaya, the tallest plunge falls) and Chitrakote (Chhattisgarh).",["waterfalls in india","highest waterfall in india","jog falls","hogenakkal falls","courtallam"]),
